Fix for clingox UPSTREAM-ISSUES U50: a parallel search in splitting mode leaks
the guiding paths that were split off but never taken when the search stops.

ParallelHandler::handleSplitMessage allocates a guiding path and hands it to
SharedData::pushWork, whose queue owns it until a thread takes it in
requestWork. SharedData::reset and SharedData::clearQueue delete what is left
in the queue, but reset runs only when the next search begins and SharedData
has no destructor. When the search is interrupted or terminates between the
push and the pop, the ParallelSolve that owns the SharedData is destroyed with
the path still queued, and the path and its literals are never freed. The
destructor now empties the queue. Against clingo v5.8.2; suitable for upstream.

diff --git a/clasp/src/parallel_solve.cpp b/clasp/src/parallel_solve.cpp
--- a/clasp/src/parallel_solve.cpp
+++ b/clasp/src/parallel_solve.cpp
@@ -73,6 +73,7 @@
 		State state;
 	};
 	SharedData() : path(0) { reset(0); control = 0; }
+	~SharedData() { clearQueue(); }
 	void reset(SharedContext* a_ctx) {
 		clearQueue();
 		syncT.reset();
